course: dictionary
lesson: 12347
title: Rude slang: recognise it, choose better words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are rude slang. You may hear them in films, from older people, or in some books, but they are not words to use at school or in your writing. Knowing what they mean helps you understand what people are saying, even when you choose different words yourself. «That's a load of crap» means «that's a load of nonsense», which is untrue or silly talk.
explain: Context helps you here. «This game is crap, let's turn it off» shows the speaker does not enjoy it. Crap means very bad or of poor quality. When someone shouts «Crap!» after something goes wrong, the word shows anger or disappointment, not that they are going to the toilet.
explain: Use the swap check. Try a school-friendly word in place of crap, such as rubbish, nonsense or poor. If your swap fits the sentence, you have understood the meaning, and you can explain it in your own clear words.
fact: «Crap» is rude slang, so do not use it at school or in your writing.
fact: «Crap» can mean nonsense or untrue things, as in «a load of crap».
fact: «Crap» can mean very bad or of poor quality, as in «a crap film».
fact: «Crap» can mean rubbish or junk, as in «clear all that crap off the table».
fact: «Crap!» is said when something goes wrong, and it shows anger or disappointment.
exercise: «That's a load of crap, he never went to the moon.» What does crap mean here? | Very large | *Nonsense, untrue talk | Happy and loud | A kind of bread
exercise: Your friend says, «This game is crap.» What does it mean? | Long and hard to finish | Very fast and exciting | Brand new | *Very bad, of poor quality
exercise: Should you use the word crap in your school writing? | *No, choose a school word such as rubbish or poor | Yes, because it is always polite | Yes, if the teacher is not listening | Yes, if it is in a film
test: «Clear all that crap off the table.» What is crap in this sentence? | *Rubbish or junk | A cup of tea | A pet dog | Clean water
test: Sam shouts «Crap!» when his kite crashes. What does his shout show? | Sleepiness | Hunger | Delight and joy | *Anger or disappointment
exam: A friend says «cut the crap» when you keep making excuses. What does it mean? | *Stop talking nonsense and get to the point | Ask for more food | Cut the cake into pieces | Start a long story
